#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1358
msgid "Operators"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1360
msgid "`BallFloat` implements `Add`, `Sub`, `Mul`, `Div` and `Neg`; `BallFloatDecorated` implements `Add`, `Sub`, `Mul` and `Div`. The operators call the methods of the same name."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1378
msgid "`Show` writes an interval in an exact text form."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1392
msgid "A bounded `BallFloat` prints as `center +/- radius` with both numbers in the exact `BinFloat` notation (`3p-1` is $3 \\cdot 2^{-1}$), so the text denotes exactly the stored set; an unbounded one prints as `[lo, hi]`, Empty as `[empty]`. A decorated interval appends `_` and the decoration; NaI prints as `[nai]`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1407
msgid "`Eq` and `Debug`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1425
msgid "The `Eq` implementations are derived and compare representations. For `BallFloat` and `BallFloatDecorated` this distinguishes equal sets stored with different precision tags or endpoint precisions; use `set_equal` for sets. `to_repr` gives the structural `Debug` form."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1432
msgid "`BallFloat` implements the `Floating` trait of [`def`](def.md) with `classify`, `sign`, `precision`, `with_precision` and `normalized` as described above, so the generic predicates `@def.is_finite` (bounded), `@def.is_infinite` (unbounded), `@def.is_nan` (Empty) and `@def.is_zero` (sign `Zero`, that is, contains 0) apply to intervals."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1442
msgid "Enclosure relations of `arithmetic`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1444
msgid "`BallFloat` implements the enclosure relation traits of `Luna-Flow/arithmetic`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1454
msgid "`Contains::contains(x, y)` is `y.subset(x)` (set inclusion, not the point-taking method); the others call the methods of the same name."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1457
msgid "Checked capabilities of `arithmetic`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1459
msgid "`BallFloat` implements `DivChecked`, `PowNatChecked` and `PowIntChecked`; their methods are promoted."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/ball_float.md:1471
msgid "Only `ctx.precision` is used: the operands are re-rounded to it with `with_precision`, the operation is applied, and the result is re-rounded. They always return `Ok`. `div_checked` follows the division rules above (a divisor containing 0 gives an unbounded result, not an error). `pow_int_checked` uses `pown`. `pow_nat_checked` uses binary powering by repeated interval multiplication, which treats the factors as independent: for an argument containing 0 its result is wider than `pown`."
msgstr ""

