#: manual/api/doc_examples.md:1
msgid "doc_examples API"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/doc_examples.md:3
msgid "`doc_examples` is a test-only package. Its only source is `src/doc_examples/README.mbt.md`, whose `moonbit check` blocks are compiled and run as tests; it exports no MoonBit items. The blocks are short, executable versions of the main workflows of the public packages (binary contexts and interchange, GDA sticky status, IEEE decimal flags, intervals and decorations, checked pipelines, semantic comparison, `numeric_expr`, and the four conformance frontends). See the [tutorial](../tutorial/doc_examples.md) and the [design page](../design/doc_examples.md)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:1
msgid "frontend/gda_expr API"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:3
msgid "`frontend/gda_expr` reads General Decimal Arithmetic test files (the `.decTest` format of Cowlishaw's decimal specification) and executes their rows against `decimal_gda`. Parsing turns every row into a `GdaCase` with its context and a [`numeric_expr`](../numeric_expr.md) expression; execution evaluates the expression and compares the result and the status flags with the row. The package does no file or process IO; the command-line runner is [`cli/gda_expr_cli`](../cli/gda_expr_cli.md). The [tutorial](../../tutorial/frontend/gda_expr.md) shows the workflow and the [design page](../../design/frontend/gda_expr.md) specifies the row mapping and the pass rule."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:22
#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:18
#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:126
msgid "Parsing"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:26
msgid "`parse_dectest(source, text)` parses a whole `.decTest` document."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:32
msgid ""
"`source` is a name used in spans (normally the file path) and `text` is the file content. The text is split at `\\n"
"`; line numbers start at 1. Each line is handled as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:36
msgid "`--` outside quotes starts a comment; the rest of the line is dropped. Leading and trailing white space is trimmed and empty lines are skipped."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:38
msgid "A line without `->` outside quotes is a directive `name: value`. The name is compared case-insensitively with `-`, `_`, spaces and tabs removed: `precision`, `rounding`, `minexponent`, `maxexponent`, `clamp`, `extended` and `dectest` update the context; `version` and unknown names are ignored. `precision`, `minExponent` and `maxExponent` must be integers, otherwise the line is a diagnostic. `clamp` is on only for the value `1`; `extended` is off only for the value `0`. A line without `:` is a diagnostic."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:46
msgid "A line with `->` is a test row. The left side is tokenized into `id operation operand…` (at least two tokens), the right side into `expected condition…` (at least one token). Tokens are separated by spaces, tabs or line breaks; a token enclosed in `'…'` or `\"…\"` may contain spaces and loses its quotes. An unterminated quote after `->` is the diagnostic `unterminated quoted token`; a quote opened before `->` hides the arrow, so the line is reported as `expected directive or testcase row`. Fewer tokens than required give `malformed testcase row`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:55
msgid "The result is `Ok(document)` when no diagnostic was produced, and otherwise `Err` with every diagnostic of the document in line order."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:58
msgid "Documents and rows"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:62
msgid "`GdaDocument` is a parsed file: its source name and its rows in file order."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:72
msgid "These methods return the source name, a copy of the rows and the number of rows."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:83
msgid "`GdaCase` is one test row together with the context in force on its line."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:93
msgid "These methods return the row id, the operation as written, and the operation name used for dispatch: lower case, with `-`, `_`, spaces and tabs removed."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:104
msgid "These methods return the operand tokens, the expected-result token and the condition tokens, unquoted and otherwise exactly as written."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:113
msgid "The arrays are copies."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:117
msgid "These methods return the directive context of the row, its span (source, line, column 1), and the row as an expression."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:126
msgid "The expression is `Expr::invoke(Operation::new(normalized_operation), …)` applied to one `Expr::literal` per operand, all carrying the row's span."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:131
msgid "`GdaContext` is the directive state of a document at a given row."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:139
msgid "It is a record of the directive values as written, not a `@decimal_gda.GdaContext`; execution converts it."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:144
msgid "`GdaContext::default()` is the context before the first directive."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:150
msgid "Precision 34, rounding `\"half_even\"`, `min_exponent` $-999999999$, `max_exponent` $999999999$, `clamp` off, `extended` on, `dectest` empty."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:155
msgid "These accessors return the directive values."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:167
msgid "`rounding` is the directive text as written (for example `\"half_up\"` or `\"05up\"`); it is only interpreted at execution time."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:172
msgid "`ParseDiagnostic` is one parse error with its location."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:182
msgid "These methods return the location (source, line, column 1) and the message, for example `\"unterminated quoted token\"`, `\"malformed testcase row\"`, `\"expected directive or testcase row\"` or `\"invalid precision directive\"`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:215
#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:74
#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:190
msgid "Execution"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:219
msgid "`execute_documents(documents, options?)` executes the selected rows of the documents, in order, and summarizes the results."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:226
msgid "Rows are visited document by document in file order. A row whose id does not match `options.case_filter()` is ignored entirely; the remaining rows are numbered $0, 1, 2, \\dots$ and row $k$ is executed when $k \\bmod n = i$ for shard count $n$ and shard index $i$. Each executed row first gets a disposition:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:232
msgid "`Diagnostic` if an operand is exactly `#` or `?`, or the expected result is exactly `#`;"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:234
msgid "`Unsupported` if a condition is not one of the thirteen GDA conditions, the operation is not implemented, or the rounding directive is not recognized;"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:237
msgid "`Executable` otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:239
msgid "Only `Executable` rows are evaluated. The row passes when the result matches the expected token and the raised conditions are exactly the listed ones; the [design page](../../design/frontend/gda_expr.md#the-pass-rule) gives the full rule. Non-executable rows get `passed() == false` and the message `\"skipped\"`, and are counted as skipped, not failed. The function never aborts on row content."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:248
msgid "`RunOptions` selects which rows `execute_documents` runs."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:258
msgid "`RunOptions::new(shard_count?, shard_index?, strict_supported?, case_filter?)` builds the options."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:265
msgid "Defaults: one shard, index 0, `strict_supported` off, empty filter (all rows). Aborts unless `shard_count > 0` and `0 <= shard_index < shard_count`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:268
msgid "`case_filter` is a comma-separated list of selectors, each trimmed. A selector `id` matches that id exactly. A selector `first..last` matches every id that has the same length as `first` and `last` and lies between them in string order, so `add001..add099` selects a numbered block."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:273
msgid "`strict_supported` is stored for callers; `execute_documents` itself does not read it. The CLI uses it to turn unsupported rows into a failing exit code."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:278
msgid "These accessors return the option values."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:287
#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:137
#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:235
#: manual/getting_started.md:13
msgid "Results"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:291
msgid "`CaseDisposition` says whether a row was executed and, if not, why."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:302
msgid "The string is a short reason such as `\"diagnostic interchange/non-scalar row\"` or `\"unsupported operation frobnicate\"`. `Legacy` exists for the shared result model; the current executor never assigns it."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:309
msgid "`CaseResult` is the outcome of one selected row."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:319
msgid "These methods return the row id, its disposition, whether it passed, and a message: empty for a pass, `\"skipped\"` for a non-executable row, `\"evaluation failed\"` when an operand could not be decoded or the operation rejected its operands, and otherwise a `\"result mismatch: expected …, actual …\"` or `\"status flags mismatch: expected …, actual …\"` text."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:335
msgid "`RunSummary` aggregates the results of a run."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:343
msgid "`RunSummary` counters"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:345
msgid "These methods return the counts of a run."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:359
msgid "`total_cases` counts the rows that match the filter (in all shards); `selected_cases` the rows executed by this shard. They satisfy"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:372
msgid "`results` returns a copy of the per-row results in execution order; `success` is true when no executable row failed."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:380
msgid "Skipped rows do not affect `success`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:384
msgid "`RunSummary::merge(parts)` combines the summaries of the shards of one run."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:390
msgid "All counters except `total_cases` are added; `total_cases` is the maximum of the parts (every shard reports the same total). Results are concatenated in the order of `parts`. Merging the $n$ shards of a run gives the same counters as an unsharded run."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:419
msgid "`GdaContext`, `ParseDiagnostic` and `RunOptions` equality and `Debug`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/gda_expr.md:421
msgid "These methods compare all fields and render the value for `Debug`. Use `==`, `!=` and `debug_inspect` in new code."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:1
msgid "frontend/itl_expr API"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:3
msgid "`frontend/itl_expr` parses interval test cases in the ITL format of the ITF1788 suite (test data for the IEEE 1788-2015 interval standard) and executes them against `ball_float`. It is a pure library: the command-line runner is [`cli/itl_expr_cli`](../cli/itl_expr_cli.md). The [tutorial](../../tutorial/frontend/itl_expr.md) walks through the workflow and the [design page](../../design/frontend/itl_expr.md) gives the pass rule."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:22
msgid "`parse_itl(source)` parses ITL text into cases."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:28
msgid "The text is read line by line, each line trimmed:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:30
msgid "lines starting with `//` and empty lines are skipped; a line starting with `/*` starts a block comment that ends on the first later line containing `*/` (or on the same line);"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:33
msgid "`testcase NAME …` starts a new block; `NAME` is the word after `testcase` and must be followed by a space, otherwise the diagnostic `\"invalid testcase declaration\"` is recorded; the statement counter restarts at 0;"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:37
msgid "a line equal to `}` is skipped;"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:38
msgid "every other line is appended (with a space) to the current statement, and a line ending in `;` completes it."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:41
msgid "A completed statement `left = expected` is split at the first `=`. The left side is split into words at spaces and tabs outside square brackets; the first word is the operation and the rest are operands. The case id is `NAME:k`, where `k` counts statements in the block from 1 (statements before the first `testcase` use the name `anonymous`). A statement without `=` or without an operation is a diagnostic `\"NAME:k: missing '='\"` or `\"NAME:k: missing operation\"`; text left after the last `;` gives `\"unterminated ITL statement\"`. The result is `Ok(cases)` when there is no diagnostic and `Err(diagnostics)` otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:53
msgid "`ItlCase` is one parsed statement."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:63
msgid "These methods return the id `NAME:k`, the operation word, a copy of the operand words and the expected text (trimmed, including any decoration suffix)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:78
msgid "`execute_case(case, precision?)` executes one case and returns its result."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:84
msgid "`precision` (default `53`) is the bit precision used to read bounds. Interval results are rounded with `@ball_float.BallContext::binary64()` regardless of `precision`, so the default is the meaningful value for ITF1788 data."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:89
msgid "Operands and expected values are read as follows. An interval literal is `[lo,hi]`, `[empty]`, `[entire]` or `[nai]`, optionally followed by `_dec` with `dec` one of `com`, `dac`, `def`, `trv`, `ill` (default `com`). A bound is `inf`/`infinity` with an optional sign, a hexadecimal float `0x…p…`, or decimal text. Decimal and hexadecimal bounds are rounded to nearest-even at `precision` bits."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:96
msgid "The case is dispatched on its operation and expected value:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:98
#: manual/performance_audit.md:25
msgid "Expected"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:98
#: manual/numeric_semantics.md:542
msgid "Comparison"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:100
#: manual/design/frontend/gda_expr.md:94
msgid "boolean"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:100
msgid "`true` or `false`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:100
msgid "equal booleans"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:101
msgid "overlap"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:101
msgid "an overlap state name (`before`, `meets`, `overlaps`, `starts`, `containedBy`, `finishes`, `equals`, `after`, `metBy`, `overlappedBy`, `startedBy`, `contains`, `finishedBy`, `bothEmpty`, `firstEmpty`, `secondEmpty`, `undefined`)"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:101
msgid "equal names"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:102
msgid "numeric"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:102
msgid "a bound"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:102
msgid "equal numbers"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:103
msgid "unary"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:103
#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:104
#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:105
#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:106
msgid "interval"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:103
#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:104
#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:105
#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:106
msgid "equal sets"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:104
msgid "ternary"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:105
msgid "integer power"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:105
msgid "`pown` (second operand an integer)"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:106
msgid "binary"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:108
msgid "\"Equal sets\" means: both NaI, or both empty, or equal lower bounds and equal upper bounds (compared numerically, so $-0 = +0$). When the expected text contains `_`, the decorations must also be equal. The boolean dispatch is chosen whenever the expected text is `true` or `false`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:113
msgid "Dispositions:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:115
msgid "`Executable` when the case was run; `passed()` tells the outcome;"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:116
msgid "`Unsupported(reason)` for an unknown operation, a binary-dispatch case whose expected value is not an interval (for example one followed by a `signal` annotation), a binary-dispatch case with other than two operands, or a binary boolean predicate whose second operand is missing or unreadable;"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:120
msgid "`Diagnostic(reason)` when the first operand of a boolean case, or an operand or the expected value of the overlap, numeric, unary, ternary or integer-power dispatch, cannot be read, or an operand of the binary dispatch is not an interval literal."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:125
msgid "`execute_case` does not abort on case content."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:129
msgid "`summarize_results(results)` counts a list of results."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:135
msgid "`total_cases` is the length of the list."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:141
msgid "`ItlDisposition` says whether a case was executed."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:153
msgid "`ItlResult` is the outcome of one case."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:163
msgid "These methods return the case id, the disposition, whether the case passed, and a message: empty on success, `\"expected E, got A\"` on a mismatch (intervals printed by `BallFloatDecorated::to_string`), and a short reason or the offending text otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:177
msgid "`RunSummary` aggregates a list of results."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:185
msgid "`RunSummary` counters and results"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:187
msgid "These methods return the counts, a copy of the results, and the overall verdict."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:201
msgid "$\\text{total} = \\text{executable} + \\text{unsupported} + \\text{diagnostic}$ and $\\text{executable} = \\text{passed} + \\text{failed}$. `success()` is true when no executable case failed **and** there is no diagnostic case; unsupported cases do not affect it."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/itl_expr.md:228
msgid "These methods compare all fields of two cases and render a case for `Debug`. Use `==`, `!=` and `debug_inspect` in new code."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:1
msgid "frontend/mpfr_expr API"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:3
msgid "`frontend/mpfr_expr` parses reference data produced with GNU MPFR and executes it against `bin_float`. Three formats are supported: MPFR's square-root `data_check` files, integer-power rows, and an elementary-function matrix with exception flags. The package does no IO; the runner is [`cli/mpfr_expr_cli`](../cli/mpfr_expr_cli.md). See the [tutorial](../../tutorial/frontend/mpfr_expr.md) for the workflow and the [design page](../../design/frontend/mpfr_expr.md) for the pass rules."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:19
msgid "Common row syntax"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:21
msgid ""
"All three parsers split the text at `\\n"
"`, trim each line, and skip empty lines and lines starting with `#`. Fields are separated by spaces, tabs or carriage returns. Line numbers start at 1. A rounding field is one of"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:34
msgid "and a number is read by `@bin_float.BinFloat::from_hex` (`0x…p…`, `inf`, `-inf`, `nan`). Each parser returns `Ok(document)` when every line is valid and otherwise `Err` with one `ParseDiagnostic` per invalid line."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:38
msgid "Square-root data"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:42
msgid "`parse_sqrt_data(source, text)` parses rows of five fields: `input_precision output_precision rounding input expected`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:49
msgid "The input is read at `input_precision` bits and the expected value at `output_precision` bits. Row ids are `sqrt:LINE`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:54
msgid "`execute_sqrt_data(document)` computes `input.sqrt_ctx(ctx)` for every row, where `ctx` is `BinaryContext::unbounded(output_precision, rounding~)`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:61
msgid "A row passes when the result is equal (`==`) to the expected `BinFloat`. Flags are not compared."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:66
msgid "`MpfrDocument` is a parsed square-root file; `MpfrCase` is one of its rows and has no public methods."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:81
msgid "`source` returns the name given to the parser and `case_count` the number of rows."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:84
#: manual/design/decimal_gda.md:522
#: manual/tutorial/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:70
msgid "Integer powers"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:88
msgid "`parse_pow_data(source, text)` parses rows of ten fields."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:94
msgid "The fields are `precision rounding input_coefficient_hex input_exponent2 input_negative exponent expected_coefficient_hex expected_exponent2 expected_negative inexact`, where the two numbers are $(-1)^{\\text{negative}} \\cdot \\text{coefficient} \\cdot 2^{\\text{exponent2}}$, the signs and `inexact` are `0` or `1`, and `exponent` is the integer power. The input is read at 512 bits and the expected value at `precision` bits. Row ids are `pow:LINE`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:104
msgid "`execute_pow_data(document)` computes `input.pow_int_ctx(exponent, ctx)` with `ctx = BinaryContext::unbounded(precision, rounding~)`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:111
msgid "A row passes when the result is equal (`==`) to the expected value, the inexact flag equals the row's flag, and no underflow, overflow, division by zero or invalid flag is raised."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:117
msgid "`MpfrPowDocument` is a parsed power file; `MpfrPowCase` is one row and has no public methods."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:136
msgid "`parse_elementary_data(source, text)` parses rows of ten fields: `op precision rounding x y n expected inexact invalid divbyzero`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:143
msgid "`op` is one of `exp`, `exp2`, `exp10`, `expm1`, `ln`, `log2`, `log10`, `log1p`, `sqrt`, `rootn`, `pown`, `pow`, `hypot`, `sin`, `cos`, `tan`, `sinpi`, `cospi`, `tanpi`, `asin`, `acos`, `atan`, `atan2`, `sinh`, `cosh`, `tanh`, `asinh`, `acosh`, `atanh`. `x` and `y` are operands read at 512 bits (`y` is `-` when unused), `n` is the integer argument of `rootn` and `pown`, `expected` is read at `precision` bits, and the last three fields are `0` or `1`. Row ids are `op:LINE`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:151
msgid "The parser does not check that `y` is present for the two-operand functions `pow`, `hypot` and `atan2`; executing such a row with `y = -` aborts."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:156
msgid "`execute_elementary_data(document)` evaluates every row with the checked `try_*_ctx` method of `BinFloat` for its operation (`sqrt_ctx` and `pown_ctx` for `sqrt` and `pown`) in `BinaryContext::unbounded(precision, rounding~)`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:164
msgid "A row passes when the result compares equal to the expected value (`compare == 0`: $+0 = -0$ and every NaN equals every NaN), the inexact, invalid and division-by-zero flags equal the row's flags, and neither underflow nor overflow is raised. If a `try_*_ctx` method returns `Err` (for example a certification failure) the row fails with the message `\"certification failure for MPFR differential case\"`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:173
msgid "`MpfrElementaryDocument` is a parsed elementary file."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:183
msgid "Diagnostics and results"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:187
#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:179
msgid "`ParseDiagnostic` is one invalid line."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:198
msgid "Messages name the problem, for example `\"MPFR pow row must contain ten fields\"`, `\"invalid MPFR pow field\"` or `\"invalid MPFR elementary expected value\"`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:204
msgid "`CaseResult` is the outcome of one row."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:215
msgid "The message is empty for a pass and otherwise shows expected and actual values in hexadecimal (and the compared flags for power and elementary rows)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:220
msgid "`RunSummary` aggregates the rows of one document."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:233
msgid "Every row is executed, so $\\text{total} = \\text{passed} + \\text{failed}$; `success` is true when no row failed. `results` returns the results in row order."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/mpfr_expr.md:256
msgid "These methods compare location and message and render a diagnostic for `Debug`. Use `==`, `!=` and `debug_inspect` in new code."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:1
msgid "frontend/testfloat_expr API"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:3
msgid "`frontend/testfloat_expr` parses Berkeley TestFloat test vectors and executes them against `bin_float` in the binary16, binary32, binary64 and binary128 interchange formats. A `TestFloatSpec` describes the function, rounding mode, tininess rule and exactness that produced a vector file; `parse_testfloat` reads the vectors and `execute_document` runs them. The package does no IO; the runner is [`cli/testfloat_expr_cli`](../cli/testfloat_expr_cli.md). The [tutorial](../../tutorial/frontend/testfloat_expr.md) shows the workflow and the [design page](../../design/frontend/testfloat_expr.md) specifies the pass rule."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:21
msgid "Function specification"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:25
msgid "`TestFloatOperation` lists the TestFloat functions the executor supports."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:50
msgid "TestFloat name"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:50
msgid "Operands"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:50
msgid "`bin_float` method"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:56
msgid "`to_integral_exact_ctx` if exact, else `to_integral_value_ctx`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:57
msgid "`to_int_ctx`, `to_int64_ctx`, `to_uint_ctx`, `to_uint64_ctx` with `exact~`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:63
msgid "`TestFloatSpec` is the configuration of one TestFloat run."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:73
msgid "`TestFloatSpec::parse(function_name, rounding, tininess?, exact?)` builds a specification from TestFloat names."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:80
msgid "`function_name` is `FORMAT_OPERATION`: the part before the first `_` is the format (`f16`, `f32`, `f64`, `f128`) and the rest is the operation (`add`, `mulAdd`, `to_ui64`, `le_quiet`, …). Names are matched case-insensitively with `-`, `_` and spaces removed. `rounding` is one of `rnear_even`, `rnear_maxMag`, `rminMag`, `rmin`, `rmax` (also accepted without the leading `r`, or as the IEEE names `roundTiesToEven`, `roundTiesToAway`, `roundTowardZero`, `roundTowardNegative`, `roundTowardPositive`). `tininess` is `\"after\"` (default) or `\"before\"` (also `tininessAfter`, `tininessBefore`). `exact` (default `false`) selects TestFloat's `-exact` variants of `roundToInt` and the integer conversions. Errors are `\"unsupported TestFloat function name …\"`, `\"… format …\"`, `\"… operation …\"`, `\"… rounding mode …\"` and `\"… tininess mode …\"`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:113
msgid "These accessors return the parsed configuration."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:124
msgid "`function_name` is the name as given."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:130
msgid "`parse_testfloat(source, text, spec)` parses the vectors of one function."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:136
msgid "Lines are trimmed; empty lines and lines starting with `#` are skipped. A vector has $k + 2$ white-space separated fields, where $k$ is the operand count of the operation: $k$ operand encodings, the expected result and a two-digit hexadecimal flag mask. Operand encodings are hexadecimal bit patterns of `spec.format()`. The expected result is an encoding for arithmetic operations, a hexadecimal integer of at most 16 digits for conversions, and `0` or `1` for comparisons. A wrong field count gives `\"unexpected TestFloat field count\"`, an unreadable field `\"invalid TestFloat hexadecimal field\"`. The result is `Ok` only when no line is invalid."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:149
msgid "`TestFloatDocument` is a parsed vector file."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:161
msgid "`cases` returns a copy of the vectors in file order."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:165
msgid "`TestFloatCase` is one vector."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:175
msgid "The id is `FUNCTION:LINE`, for example `f64_mulAdd:17`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:194
msgid "`execute_document(document, options?)` executes the selected vectors."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:200
msgid "Vector $k$ (counting from 0 in file order) is executed when $k \\bmod n = i$ for shard count $n$ and index $i$. Operands are decoded to `BinFloat` and the operation runs in `spec.format().context(rounding~, tininess~)`. The vector passes when:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:205
msgid "**arithmetic:** the result, re-encoded in the format with the same rounding and tininess, has exactly the expected bit pattern, or the expected result is any NaN and the actual result is a quiet NaN; and the SoftFloat mask of the operation's flags combined with the encoding flags equals the expected mask;"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:210
msgid "**integer conversion:** if the expected mask has the invalid bit `10`, the conversion must report invalid (`None`) and its value field is ignored; otherwise the conversion must return the expected integer (signed results compared as two's-complement bit patterns); in both cases the flag masks must be equal;"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:215
msgid "**comparison:** the boolean and the flag mask are equal."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:217
msgid "Every selected vector is executable; there are no skipped vectors."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:221
msgid "`RunOptions` selects a shard."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:232
msgid "Defaults: one shard, index 0. `RunOptions::new` aborts unless `shard_count > 0` and `0 <= shard_index < shard_count`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:239
msgid "`CaseResult` is the outcome of one vector."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:250
msgid "Messages: empty for a pass; `\"value mismatch: expected HEX, actual HEX\"`, `\"integer mismatch: …\"`, `\"comparison mismatch: …\"`, or `\"flags mismatch: expected M, actual M\"` (masks in decimal)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:256
msgid "`RunSummary` aggregates a run."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:270
msgid "`total_cases` is the number of vectors in the document, `selected_cases = passed_cases + failed_cases` the number executed by this shard, and `success` is true when none failed."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:276
msgid "Equality and `Debug` of `TestFloatOperation`, `TestFloatSpec` and `ParseDiagnostic`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/frontend/testfloat_expr.md:278
