#: manual/design/semantic.md:3
msgid "Design goal"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:11
msgid "A floating-point computation returns a number near the true result, with an error that the caller has to estimate separately. `ball_float` returns an interval that provably contains the true result, at any working precision, so that the error bound is part of the value. Three requirements follow:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:16
msgid "**Inclusion before tightness.** Every operation returns a superset of the exact image of its operands. A wider result is acceptable; a result that misses a possible value is a bug."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/ball_float.md:19
msgid "**Explicit semantics.** Precision, target format, flags and decorations are values passed in and returned, never process-global state (no hardware rounding-mode switching)."
msgstr ""

