#: manual/performance_audit.md:43
msgid "A remainder-only kernel returns the same $r$ as a quotient-and-remainder kernel, so it preserves every observable remainder and every step of the Euclidean algorithm. The GDA half-power predicate compares $a$ with $5 \\cdot 10^{\\,\\operatorname{digits}(a) - 1}$ by its leading decimal digit and whether its tail is non-zero; it is exact, not a floating estimate."
msgstr ""

#: manual/performance_audit.md:49
msgid "The IEEE decimal exact-division path first divides out $g = \\gcd(c_x, c_y)$. A quotient $c_x / c_y$ has a finite decimal expansion exactly when the reduced denominator $c_y / g$ has no prime factor other than 2 and 5:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/performance_audit.md:59
msgid "The path is taken only then. It builds the exact coefficient and exponent and calls the existing finalizer; any unmet factor, bound or special-value precondition returns to the generic algorithm. The optimization changes the route to the exact value, not the IEEE rounding or flag rule."
msgstr ""

#: manual/performance_audit.md:64
msgid "Binary contextual paths"
msgstr ""

#: manual/performance_audit.md:66
msgid "For a finite dyadic value $c \\cdot 2^{e}$, `binary_exact_top(c, e)` is the exponent of the highest set bit, $e + \\operatorname{bitlen}(c) - 1$. Comparing these tops is equivalent to comparing magnitudes before alignment, including coefficients with different trailing powers of two. When a far addend is discarded, the split keeps the first discarded bit (the round bit) and the OR of all later bits (the sticky bit). These are exactly the inputs of the rounding decision: for the truncated magnitude $t$ and the discarded fraction $f \\in [0, 1)$ of one ulp,"
msgstr ""

#: manual/performance_audit.md:80
msgid "and every IEEE rounding direction is a function of $t$'s last bit, the sign, and these two bits. The fast path therefore feeds the same rounding inputs while never materializing an enormous aligned coefficient."
msgstr ""

#: manual/performance_audit.md:84
msgid "Directed interval paths"
msgstr ""

#: manual/performance_audit.md:86
