msgid "Common pitfalls"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:362
msgid "**`x - x` is not zero.** Interval arithmetic treats the two operands as independent unknowns, so $[1, 2] - [1, 2] = [-1, 1]$. The same holds for `x * x`, which is wider than `x.square()` when `x` contains zero:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:380
msgid "Rewrite expressions so that each uncertain quantity appears once, and prefer `square`, `pown` and the elementary functions over hand-written products."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:383
msgid "**`==` is not set equality.** `==` compares the stored representation, including the precision tag; use `set_equal` to compare sets."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:386
msgid "**`contains` takes a point.** The method `BallFloat::contains` tests a `BinFloat` point. Set inclusion is `subset` (or the trait method `@lf_arith.Contains::contains`, which means \"contains as a subset\")."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:390
msgid "**Intervals are not ordered.** There is no total order on intervals; never sort them with `less` (an IEEE 1788 set relation) as if it were a comparison of numbers."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:394
msgid "**Unbounded intervals have no center.** `center()`, `radius()` and `midpoint()` abort on the empty set and on half-bounded intervals (`midpoint()` returns 0 for the whole line). Check `is_bounded()` first, or use `radius_extended()`, which returns $+\\infty$ instead."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:399
msgid "**Integers wider than the precision.** `from_int(n, precision=p)` and `from_coefficient` currently round `n` to the nearest value with $\\max(p, 8)$ bits before building the interval, so for an integer wider than that the result can miss `n`. Use a precision at least as large as the bit length of the integer (the default of 16 bits only covers $|n| < 2^{16}$)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:405
msgid "[!WARNING] `BallFloat::from_int(257, precision=8)` is the singleton $\\{256\\}$ on the current branch. Build such values with `from_bounds` on directed roundings, or use enough precision."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float.md:410
msgid "**Inputs from `Double`.** `from_double(x)` encloses the binary value of `x` exactly; it cannot know which decimal number `x` approximated. Enclose decimal data as in [Enclose a decimal constant](#enclose-a-decimal-constant)."
msgstr ""

