#: manual/tutorial/ball_float_checked.md:219
msgid "**Small default precision.** `from_int` and `from_coefficient` default to 16 bits. On the current branch an integer that needs more bits is rounded to nearest *before* it is enclosed, so `from_int(100001)` does not contain $100001$. Pass `precision=53` (or more) for large integers."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float_checked.md:223
msgid "**Empty and whole are successes.** Test `is_empty` / `is_entire` on the final interval, or add a `bind` check."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/ball_float_checked.md:225
msgid "**No decorations or flags.** The wrapper keeps neither IEEE 1788 decorations nor `BallFlags`; use the decorated and contextual APIs of `ball_float` when you need them."
