msgid "[`decimal_checked` tutorial](decimal_checked.md) and [`decimal_gda` tutorial](decimal_gda.md) for pipelines and GDA status."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:1
msgid "`decimal_checked` tutorial"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:3
msgid "This tutorial shows how to run an IEEE decimal calculation as one pipeline that remembers every exceptional condition: you fix a `DecimalContext`, start a `DecimalChecked` from a string or number, apply operations, and at the end read the value together with the union of all flags raised on the way. The typical use is an auditable calculation (money, measurements) where \"was anything rounded?\" or \"did anything overflow?\" must be answered for the whole computation, not for the last step. Arithmetic comes from [`decimal`](decimal.md); the [design page](../design/decimal_checked.md) gives the algebra of flag accumulation; the [API reference](../api/decimal_checked.md) lists every method."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:27
msgid "Divide 10 by 4 in decimal64 and check that the result is exact:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:63
msgid "Audit a price calculation"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:65
msgid "Compute a price with tax, rounded to cents. `raised()` describes the last step and `flags()` the whole pipeline:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:81
msgid "The multiplication is exact ($19.99 \\times 1.0825 = 21.639175$); only the quantization to cents rounds, and the pipeline records that."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:84
msgid "Find out that an earlier step rounded"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:86
msgid "Flags of earlier steps stay in `flags()` even when later steps are exact:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:101
msgid "Keep going after a division by zero"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:103
msgid "IEEE decimal arithmetic defines a result for every operation. Dividing by zero gives an infinity and the `division_by_zero` flag; the pipeline continues and the flag is kept:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:120
msgid "Decide at the end what the flags mean for your application, for example with `DecimalFlags::has_error`, which is true when any of `invalid_operation`, `division_by_zero`, `division_impossible`, `division_undefined` or `invalid_context` is set."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:125
msgid "Start a new audit period"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:127
msgid "`clear_flags` resets both the raised and the accumulated flags without touching the value:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:144
msgid "Multiplying the 16-digit quotient by ten is exact, so the second phase reports no flags although the first one rounded."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:149
msgid "Elementary functions need a bounded context"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:151
msgid "Mathematical functions (`exp`, `ln`, `power`, the trigonometric family, …) follow the General Decimal Arithmetic restriction to precision and exponent limits within $\\pm 999\\,999$. Use one of the interchange contexts or explicit bounds; with the default unbounded range they return NaN with `invalid_context`:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:173
msgid "Start from a Luna-Flow/arithmetic context"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:175
msgid "Code that is generic over Luna-Flow/arithmetic carries an `ArithmeticContext`. `DecimalContext::from_arithmetic_context` maps its precision, rounding direction, exponent bounds and clamp flag; the predefined `ArithmeticContext::decimal64()` maps to the same context as `DecimalContext::decimal64()`:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:193
msgid "Hand the result to the contextual traits"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:195
msgid "`result()` returns `Ok((value, flags))` or the recorded error. The `AddContextual`, `SqrtContextual`, … implementations of `Decimal` in Luna-Flow/arithmetic report diagnostics instead of flags; the six shared conditions (`inexact`, `rounded`, `overflow`, `underflow`, `subnormal`, `clamped`) can be carried over field by field:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:227
msgid "The [design page](../design/decimal_checked.md#from-flags-to-arithmetic-diagnostics) shows why converting the accumulated flags once gives the same diagnostics as combining the per-step diagnostics."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:233
msgid "**`raised()` is not the whole story.** It describes the latest step only; audit with `flags()`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:235
msgid "**Exceptional results are not errors.** NaN, infinities and rounded values are successes with flags. `is_err()` is true only for certification failures of elementary functions."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:238
msgid "**Unbounded contexts disable the mathematical functions.** See above; this also applies to contexts built from an `ArithmeticContext` without `e_min` / `e_max`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:241
msgid "**Binary sources.** `from_double(0.1, …)` converts the binary value of `0.1` (via 17 digits), not one tenth; parse the string `\"0.1\"` instead."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:243
msgid "**Operands are plain `Decimal` values.** They are not rounded to the context before the operation; the operation rounds the result."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:245
msgid "**`clear_flags` also works after an error,** but the error stays."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:249
msgid "[`decimal_checked` design](../design/decimal_checked.md): the state model, the flag monoid and the short-circuit rule."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:251
msgid "[`decimal_checked` API](../api/decimal_checked.md): every method."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_checked.md:252
msgid "[`decimal` tutorial](decimal.md): contexts, rounding modes and interchange formats."
msgstr ""

