msgid "[`decimal` tutorial](decimal.md): the IEEE 754 decimal model with per-operation flags."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:1
msgid "`decimal_gda_checked` tutorial"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:3
msgid "This tutorial shows how to run a General Decimal Arithmetic (GDA) calculation as a pipeline that honours GDA traps: you choose a `GdaContext` with the traps your application needs, start a `GdaDecimalChecked`, chain operations, detect the step that trapped, inspect the sticky status, and decide explicitly whether to continue. This is the model of Python's `decimal` module and of the GDA test suites: status flags are sticky, and an enabled trap stops the computation. The operations come from [`decimal_gda`](decimal_gda.md); the [design page](../design/decimal_gda_checked.md) proves the status and trap laws; the [API reference](../api/decimal_gda_checked.md) lists every method."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:26
msgid "Divide under the GDA *basic* context, which traps division by zero:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:63
msgid "Choose the traps"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:65
msgid "A `GdaContext` carries a trap set. The predefined contexts differ: `GdaContext::default()` (the GDA basic context: precision 9, `HalfUp`) traps `DivisionByZero`, `InvalidOperation`, `Overflow`, `Underflow` and `Clamped`; `decimal32()`, `decimal64()`, `decimal128()` and `new(...)` trap nothing. Add or remove traps with `trap`:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:93
msgid "Read the sticky status"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:95
msgid "`raised()` holds the signals of the latest operation, `status()` every signal since the context was created:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:111
msgid "Nothing runs after a trap"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:113
msgid "Once trapped, every further operation returns the pipeline unchanged; the value is the defined result of the trapped step:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:129
msgid "Resume deliberately"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:131
msgid "`resume_defined()` accepts the defined result and continues. The status still records the trapped signal, so the decision is visible afterwards:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:148
msgid "The traps are still enabled after resuming: dividing by zero again traps again."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:153
msgid "Syntax errors are invalid operations"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:155
msgid "GDA classifies conversion syntax, impossible and undefined divisions and invalid contexts as *invalid-operation conditions*. A context that traps `InvalidOperation` therefore stops on a malformed string, and the status gains `invalid_operation` next to the specific condition:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:176
msgid "Mathematical functions need bounded contexts"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:178
msgid "`exp`, `ln`, `log10` and `power` follow the GDA restriction to precision and exponent limits within $\\pm 999\\,999$. The interchange contexts satisfy it; `GdaContext::new` with its default unbounded range does not, and the functions return NaN with `invalid_context` (which traps under `InvalidOperation`):"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:200
msgid "Combine with the plain GDA functions"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:202
msgid "Any `decimal_gda` operation returns a `GdaOutcome`. When the pipeline has no method for it, run it on `value()` and `context()` and wrap the outcome:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:217
msgid "Do this only on a pipeline that is not trapped; `from_outcome` does not check the previous state."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:222
msgid "**`default()` traps, `new()` does not.** Choose the context deliberately."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:223
msgid "**`raised()` versus `status()`.** The first is the latest step, the second the sticky history."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:225
msgid "**`resume_defined` keeps the status and the traps.** It clears only the trap marker and `raised()`. Clear the status with `GdaContext::clear_status` on a context and start a new pipeline if needed."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:228
msgid "**No errors.** Traps are not converted to `ArithmeticError`; check `is_trapped()`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:230
msgid "**Two decimal packages.** `decimal_gda.Decimal` is not `decimal.Decimal`; IEEE-style flag accumulation without traps is [`decimal_checked`](decimal_checked.md)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:236
msgid "[`decimal_gda_checked` design](../design/decimal_gda_checked.md): sticky status as a monoid, the trap predicate and the short-circuit proof."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:238
msgid "[`decimal_gda_checked` API](../api/decimal_gda_checked.md): every method."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/decimal_gda_checked.md:239
msgid "[`decimal_gda` tutorial](decimal_gda.md): contexts, rounding modes and the full GDA operation set."
msgstr ""

