#: manual/tutorial/internal.md:33
msgid "`round_positive_div` takes the magnitude $n/d$ and the sign of the true quotient separately, because directed modes round magnitudes differently for negative numbers."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/internal.md:39
msgid "Round a decimal coefficient to `p` digits"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/internal.md:41
msgid "A decimal $c \\cdot 10^{q}$ with more than $p$ digits is rounded by dividing the coefficient by $10^{k}$, $k = \\text{digits}(c) - p$, and adding $k$ to the exponent:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/internal.md:76
msgid "A carry can produce $10^{p}$ (for example $999.6 \\to 1000$); real cores renormalize that case, which this sketch omits."
